     1	=== SVG Support ===
     2	Contributors: Benbodhi
     3	Donate link: https://www.paypal.com/cgi-bin/webscr?cmd=_s-xclick&hosted_button_id=Z9R7JERS82EQQ
     4	Tags: svg, vector, safe svg, sanitization, mime type
     5	Requires at least: 5.8
     6	Tested up to: 6.7.3
     7	Requires PHP: 7.4
     8	Stable tag: 2.5.14
     9	License: GPLv2 or later
    10	License URI: http://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-2.0.html
    11	
    12	Securely upload SVG files to your media library, with built-in sanitization and advanced features for styling and animation.
    13	
    14	== Description ==
    15	
    16	**The complete SVG solution for WordPress - secure, flexible, and easy to use.**
    17	
    18	SVG Support enables secure SVG uploads with powerful features for both basic users and developers:
    19	
    20	✨ **Key Features**:
    21	- Secure SVG uploads with automatic sanitization
    22	- Inline rendering for direct CSS/JS manipulation
    23	- File size optimization through minification
    24	- Role-based access control
    25	- Advanced developer options
    26	- Multisite compatible
    27	- Full Block Editor (Gutenberg) compatibility
    28	
    29	🔒 **Security First**:
    30	- Built-in sanitization removes potentially harmful code
    31	- Role-based upload restrictions
    32	- Comprehensive MIME type validation
    33	
    34	🎨 **Designer Friendly**:
    35	- Direct styling of SVG elements
    36	- Animation support
    37	- Custom class targeting
    38	- Automatic dimension handling
    39	
    40	💻 **Developer Ready**:
    41	- Advanced mode for additional features
    42	- REST API support
    43	- Gutenberg compatible
    44	- Extensive hooks and filters
    45	
    46	
    47	== Usage ==
    48	
    49	**Basic Usage**:
    50	- First, install and activate SVG Support via your WordPress dashboard
    51	- Upload SVG files to your media library like any other image
    52	- Works seamlessly with Image blocks, Cover blocks and featured images
    53	
    54	**Advanced Usage**:
    55	- Enable "Advanced Mode" for minification and inline rendering
    56	- Customize with hooks and filters for tailored functionality
    57	
    58	**Block Editor Usage**:
    59	- Use Advanced Mode to enable inline rendering:
    60	  - Add the `"style-svg"` class to Image blocks
    61	  - Add the `"style-svg"` class to Cover blocks to render SVG backgrounds inline
    62	- Use "Skip Nested SVGs" setting to control inline rendering of SVGs within Cover blocks
    63	
    64	**Classic Editor Usage**:
    65	- Use Advanced Mode to add the `"style-svg"` class to `<img>` tags for inline rendering
    66	- Enable "Auto Insert Class" option for automatic class insertion in Classic Editor
    67	
    68	**Common Issues & Solutions**:
    69	- SVG not displaying? Ensure dimensions are set in CSS.
    70	- Need help? Use the support tab and I will do my best to assist you.
    71	
    72	
    73	== Spin up a test site ==
    74	
    75	With a single click, you can spin up a completely free test site to test SVG Support using TasteWP! No sign up, no cards, nothing! How cool is that? Give it a go:
    76	[Click Here to spin up a test site in seconds](https://tastewp.com/new?pre-installed-plugin-slug=svg-support&redirect=options-general.php%3Fpage%3Dsvg-support&ni=true)
    77	
    78	
    79	== Security ==
    80	
    81	SVG Support prioritizes security with automatic sanitization and role-based restrictions. Only trusted users should have upload permissions. Configure settings to balance functionality and security.
    82	
    83	
    84	== Feedback ==
    85	
    86	I'm open to your [suggestions and feedback](mailto:wp@benbodhi.com) - Thanks for using SVG Support!
    87	
    88	Follow [@SVGSupport](https://twitter.com/svgsupport) on Twitter
    89	Follow [@benbodhi](https://twitter.com/benbodhi) on Twitter
    90	Follow [@benbodhi](https://warpcast.com/benbodhi) on Warpcast
    91	
    92	*Note:* I hope you like this plugin! Please take a moment to [rate it](https://wordpress.org/support/view/plugin-reviews/svg-support?filter=5#postform).
    93	
    94	
    95	== Development & Contributing ==
    96	
    97	The development version of SVG Support is maintained on GitHub. Feel free to contribute:
    98	
    99	* Submit bug reports or feature suggestions: [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/benbodhi/svg-support/issues)
   100	* Contribute code via [Pull Requests](https://github.com/benbodhi/svg-support/pulls)
   101	* Development repository: [GitHub](https://github.com/benbodhi/svg-support)
   102	
   103	
   104	== Translations ==
   105	
   106	Contribute translations [here](https://translate.wordpress.org/projects/wp-plugins/svg-support). New to translating? Check the [Translator Handbook](https://make.wordpress.org/polyglots/handbook/tools/glotpress-translate-wordpress-org/).
   107	
   108	
   109	== Frequently Asked Questions ==
   110	
   111	= SVG not rendering inline since 2.3 update =
   112	Ensure "Advanced Mode" is enabled in Settings > SVG Support.
   113	
   114	= How do I disable the Javascript on the front end if I am not using inline SVG? =
   115	Disable "Advanced Mode" in the settings.
   116	
   117	= I'm trying to use SVG in the customizer but it's not working. =
   118	To allow SVG to work in the customizer, you will need to modify/add some code in your child theme's function file. [Here is a great tutorial](https://thebrandid.com/using-svg-logos-wordpress-customizer/) on how to do that. The important part is:
   119	`
   120	'flex-width'	=> true

