{
  "plugin_slug": "kubio",
  "analysis_summary": {
    "scope": "Validated Phase 1 IR and Semgrep candidates directly against Kubio 2.7.1 source, prioritizing REST/AJAX/import/file-operation paths and contributor-or-lower reachable surfaces.",
    "highlights": [
      "No Patchstack-eligible true positive was confirmed from the reviewed candidates.",
      "Most REST exposure alerts were false positives because the live routes enforce permission callbacks such as current_user_can('edit_theme_options') or controller permission methods.",
      "Two flows remain REVIEW: one multisite-oriented file-read-to-cloud-upload path in /snippet, and one demo-site plugin install/activate capability mismatch that depends on deployment role semantics."
    ]
  },
  "overall_risk": "review",
  "total_findings_analyzed": 2,
  "true_positives": 0,
  "false_positives": 0,
  "needs_review": 2,
  "findings": [
    {
      "finding_id": "KUBIO-P2-REV-001",
      "verdict": "REVIEW",
      "vuln_type": "Path Traversal to Arbitrary File Read with Second-Order Cloud Exfiltration",
      "cwe_id": "CWE-22",
      "severity": "high",
      "auth_required": "authenticated user with edit_theme_options; most relevant on multisite site-admin contexts",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "entry_point_id": "ep_rest___snippet",
      "source_function": "kubio_save_block_snippet",
      "sink_function": "kubio_create_snippet_zip",
      "source_file_path": "plugins/kubio/lib/api/colibri.php",
      "source_line_number": 112,
      "sink_file_path": "plugins/kubio/lib/api/colibri.php",
      "sink_line_number": 282,
      "file_path": "plugins/kubio/lib/api/colibri.php",
      "line_number": 282,
      "storage_key": "kubio_cloud_api_key",
      "reasoning": {
        "hypothesis": "The /snippet REST route accepts attacker-controlled snippet JSON and may treat forged upload URLs as local filesystem paths without constraining them to the uploads directory.",
        "trace": [
          "The route /snippet is registered with permission_callback current_user_can('edit_theme_options') at plugins/kubio/lib/api/colibri.php:48-57.",
          "kubio_save_block_snippet reads the untrusted request parameter snippet via get_param('snippet') at plugins/kubio/lib/api/colibri.php:112 and passes it into kubio_create_snippet_zip at plugins/kubio/lib/api/colibri.php:129.",
          "kubio_create_snippet_zip regex-parses every URL under wp_get_upload_dir()['baseurl'] from the JSON-encoded snippet at plugins/kubio/lib/api/colibri.php:263-267, concatenates each captured suffix directly onto wp_get_upload_dir()['basedir'] at plugins/kubio/lib/api/colibri.php:278-279, and reads the resolved path with file_get_contents at plugins/kubio/lib/api/colibri.php:281-284.",
          "After zipping the gathered files, kubio_save_block_snippet uploads the archive body to the snippets cloud endpoint at plugins/kubio/lib/api/colibri.php:133-151.",
          "The same edit_theme_options role can also set kubio_cloud_api_key through /kubio-api-key at plugins/kubio/lib/api/kubio-cloud.php:23-32 and plugins/kubio/lib/api/kubio-cloud.php:86-90, so the upload credential is user-controllable in the same trust boundary."
        ],
        "defenses": [
          "The destination host is fixed to Kubio cloud via KUBIO_CLOUD_URL and Utils::getSnippetsURL() at plugins/kubio/plugin.php:67-68 and plugins/kubio/lib/src/Core/Utils.php:477-485.",
          "The route is not public; it requires edit_theme_options."
        ],
        "refutation": [
          "I did not find any realpath, basename, validate_file, or prefix check that rejects .. segments before file_exists/file_get_contents is reached.",
          "The fixed host refutes generic SSRF, but it does not refute local file disclosure into the ZIP payload if an attacker-controlled or attacker-chosen kubio_cloud_api_key is accepted.",
          "What remains unproven from source alone is whether the cloud service will always accept an attacker-controlled API key and whether the uploaded ZIP can be retrieved by that same account without dynamic verification."
        ],
        "conclusion": "The local source-to-sink traversal is real in code, and the same capability boundary can set the cloud API key used for upload. Because end-to-end attacker retrieval depends on external Kubio cloud behavior not visible in this repository, I am keeping this as REVIEW instead of TP."
      },
      "poc_description": "In a multisite test where a site admin has edit_theme_options, first POST /wp-json/kubio/v1/kubio-api-key with an attacker-controlled Kubio cloud API key. Then POST /wp-json/kubio/v1/snippet with snippet JSON containing a forged URL such as https://target.example/wp-content/uploads/../../wp-config.php. The code path at kubio_create_snippet_zip will resolve the traversal path, read it into the ZIP, and send that ZIP to the snippets cloud endpoint using kubio_cloud_api_key.",
      "cvss_vector": null,
      "remediation": "Resolve candidate asset paths with realpath(), reject any path containing traversal, and enforce that the normalized path stays under wp_get_upload_dir()['basedir']. Prefer attachment-ID based resolution over raw URL scraping. If snippet uploads can move server-side file data off host, gate both /snippet and /kubio-api-key behind a stronger capability on multisite.",
      "patchstack_eligible": false
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "KUBIO-P2-REV-002",
      "verdict": "REVIEW",
      "vuln_type": "Insufficient Capability Check for Plugin Installation/Activation",
      "cwe_id": "CWE-862",
      "severity": "high",
      "auth_required": "authenticated user who can satisfy current_user_can('import') and obtain the demo-site nonce",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "entry_point_id": "ep_ajax_priv_wp_ajax_kubio_demo_site_install_plugin",
      "source_function": "Kubio\\DemoSites\\DemoSites::installPlugin",
      "sink_function": "Kubio\\PluginsManager::installPlugin",
      "source_file_path": "plugins/kubio/lib/src/DemoSites/DemoSites.php",
      "source_line_number": 331,
      "sink_file_path": "plugins/kubio/lib/src/PluginsManager.php",
      "sink_line_number": 65,
      "file_path": "plugins/kubio/lib/src/PluginsManager.php",
      "line_number": 65,
      "reasoning": {
        "hypothesis": "The demo-site AJAX flow allows plugin install/activation after only checking the import capability, not install_plugins/activate_plugins, which may be too weak on some deployments such as multisite.",
        "trace": [
          "DemoSites registers wp_ajax_kubio-demo-site-install-plugin and wp_ajax_kubio-demo-site-activate-plugin at plugins/kubio/lib/src/DemoSites/DemoSites.php:323-324.",
          "Both handlers call DemoSitesHelpers::verifyAjaxCall() first at plugins/kubio/lib/src/DemoSites/DemoSites.php:327-328 and plugins/kubio/lib/src/DemoSites/DemoSites.php:347-348.",
          "verifyAjaxCall only checks the kubio-ajax-demo-site-verification nonce and current_user_can('import') at plugins/kubio/lib/src/DemoSites/DemoSitesHelpers.php:15-19.",
          "The install handler then reads $_REQUEST['slug'] at plugins/kubio/lib/src/DemoSites/DemoSites.php:331 and passes it to PluginsManager::installPlugin at plugins/kubio/lib/src/DemoSites/DemoSites.php:337, which reaches Plugin_Upgrader->install(...) at plugins/kubio/lib/src/PluginsManager.php:48-65 without any local install_plugins check.",
          "The sibling activate handler reads $_REQUEST['slug'] at plugins/kubio/lib/src/DemoSites/DemoSites.php:351 and reaches activate_plugin(...) at plugins/kubio/lib/src/PluginsManager.php:98-105, again without any local activate_plugins check.",
          "The nonce is emitted into the starter-sites UI and inline editor data at plugins/kubio/lib/admin-pages/main-page/demo-sites.php:198-202 and plugins/kubio/lib/editor-assets.php:374-380."
        ],
        "defenses": [
          "The AJAX calls are nonce-protected.",
          "The code explicitly checks current_user_can('import')."
        ],
        "refutation": [
          "I did not find any Kubio-side current_user_can('install_plugins') or current_user_can('activate_plugins') check in this flow.",
          "I also did not find Kubio code that grants import to low roles during the normal web flow; the allowImportCaps helper is only wired in CLI-specific paths at plugins/kubio/lib/filters/wp-import.php:202-204 and plugins/kubio/lib/src/Core/Activation.php:50-52.",
          "The unresolved point is WordPress deployment semantics: if only full administrators satisfy import on the affected site, then the issue becomes admin-only; if a lower privileged actor such as a multisite site admin can satisfy import while lacking install/activate plugin privileges, the flow becomes a real privilege boundary break."
        ],
        "conclusion": "The capability mismatch is real in Kubio code, but I cannot prove from this repository alone that a Patchstack-relevant non-admin actor reaches current_user_can('import') on the target deployment. Keep as REVIEW, with multisite/site-admin validation prioritized."
      },
      "poc_description": "On a deployment where a non-super-admin role passes current_user_can('import'), obtain the kubio-ajax-demo-site-verification nonce from the starter-sites UI or localized editor data, then POST to /wp-admin/admin-ajax.php with action=kubio-demo-site-install-plugin, slug=<wordpress-org-plugin>, nonce=<nonce>. Follow with action=kubio-demo-site-activate-plugin and the same slug to test whether Kubio bypasses the normal install_plugins/activate_plugins boundary.",
      "cvss_vector": null,
      "remediation": "Require current_user_can('install_plugins') in installPlugin() and current_user_can('activate_plugins') in activatePlugin(), in addition to the existing nonce. On multisite, explicitly honor the network/site distinction before calling Plugin_Upgrader or activate_plugin.",
      "patchstack_eligible": false
    }
  ],
  "negative_findings": [
