        "plugins/kubio/lib/menu/class-wp-rest-menu-locations-controller.php:111-119"
      ],
      "reasoning": "Both controllers attach permission callbacks before read or write actions. The menu controller uses get_permissions() -> current_user_can('edit_theme_options'), and the menu-locations controller uses explicit permission-check methods that return WP_Error unless edit_theme_options is present."
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "KUBIO-P2-NEG-002",
      "verdict": "FP",
      "summary": "The get-started tab include is not a raw user-controlled LFI.",
      "evidence": [
        "plugins/kubio/lib/admin-pages/kubio-get-started.php:66-80",
        "plugins/kubio/lib/admin-pages/kubio-get-started.php:89-98"
      ],
      "reasoning": "The request only provides a sanitized tab key via sanitize_key($_REQUEST['tab']). Kubio then looks up that key in kubio_get_started_page_tabs() and uses the mapped tab-partial value. The request does not flow directly into require_once; exploitation would require a trusted filter to inject a malicious tab definition first."
    },
