      "reasoning": "If a downstream plugin or theme deliberately lowers `page_permissions`, exposes the same Redux field UIs on profile/metabox/customizer screens available to weaker roles, or otherwise leaks user-scoped nonces, the weak boolean guards documented above could become exploitable. That scenario was not reproducible in the packaged `redux-framework` plugin, so it is recorded as a framework hardening note rather than an in-scope vulnerability."
